    "result_text": "The build is green. The full suite (only `AcceptanceTest` is a runnable test class; the other files are `AcceptanceBase` and its support) passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `telephoneDisplay` read-only property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field), documented as the country code + space + national digits grouped in threes.\n\n2. **`OwnerTelephone.java`** \u2014 Added a public `toDisplay(String)` method that canonicalises to E.164, identifies the country code from the existing `NATIONAL_LENGTHS` registry (longest-prefix-first, so `61` before `1`), then renders `+<cc> <nnn> <nnn> <nnn>`. It reuses the project's single source of truth for the telephone rule and is best-effort (null\u2192null; unparseable/unknown-country values returned unchanged rather than throwing). I made the class `public` to match the already-public `OwnerIdentity`/`OwnerCustomerCode` helpers the mapper calls.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` expression deriving `telephoneDisplay` from `owner.getTelephone()` at read time, alongside the other derived fields.\n\nVerified with the acceptance test: input `0412 345 678` is stored as `telephone = \"+61412345678\"` and returned with `telephoneDisplay = \"+61 412 345 678\"`.",
