    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally clean and additive:\n\n- **Right unit.** `toDisplay` lives in `OwnerTelephone`, which the class javadoc explicitly declares the \"single source of truth for the owner telephone normalisation rule.\" Formatting-for-display is the same domain, builds on `toE164`, and sits naturally beside `toE164`/`toE164OrRaw`. It reuses the existing `NATIONAL_LENGTHS` map rather than re-deriving country codes elsewhere.\n\n- **No meaningful duplication.** The only overlap is a short country-code prefix scan also present in `toE164`, but the two loops serve different purposes (length enforcement vs. extracting the code for grouping) and extracting a shared helper would be marginal \u2014 not worth flagging.\n\n- **Idiomatic wiring.** The mapper addition mirrors the existing `identityKey` mapping exactly: a fully-qualified inline `@Mapping` expression delegating to a `public final` function class (`OwnerIdentity` is `public final` too, confirmed). The `public` visibility bump on `OwnerTelephone` is the minimal change needed for that reference, consistent with its sibling.\n\n- **Not a catch-all.** `OwnerTelephone` stays cohesive around telephone canonicalisation/formatting; the mapper gains one derived field following its established derivation convention.\n\n- **OpenAPI** documents `telephoneDisplay` as a read-only derived string alongside the existing derived fields, matching the spec's intent and example.\n\nA maintainer of this codebase would find all three edits natural.",
